;; it-fault-wrap-ld.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fault-wrap-ld.s` (P2-SCALAR.4).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-fault-wrap-ld.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-fault-wrap-ld.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fault-wrap-ld.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05), against the reference behaviors MEASURED by probe `wrap-ld` (sail-riscv 0.14 AND" "spike 1.1.1-dev) before this guest existed. Fault × boundary: the address computation wraps" "modulo 2^64 INTO the fault — 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC + 4 is address 0, and the trap's tval is the" "wrapped address, not the pre-wrap sum. x2 is never written.")
(expectations (program "it-fault-wrap-ld.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (never_written "x2") (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, -4") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC"))) (derivation "The 12-bit immediate -4 sign-extends to all ones bar the low two bits: x1 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC — the base four bytes below the wrap point.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-ALU-IMM: the immediate sign-extends)")) (step (n 1) (insn "ld x2, x1, 4") (writes) (derivation "The effective address is (rs1 + sext(imm)) mod 2^64 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC + 4 = 0 — the wrap (D-ADDR-WRAP, on the load path). Address 0 belongs to no declared region, so the load raises load-access-fault: cause 0x05, tval = 0x0000000000000000 — measured identical on both references (probe wrap-ld), and 0 < 2^56 so DIFF-TVAL-PHYS-MASK (sail's 56-bit tval masking) cannot reach it. x2 is never written.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-LUI-AUIPC); RVI-INTRO, Memory (D-ADDR-WRAP); RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-ADDRESS-SPACE)")))
